\cwm{}'s 5-seed standard deviation (0.36\pp{}) is notably lower than \cls{} (0.78\pp{}) and TRAJ (0.97\pp{}). This is consistent with the bottleneck hypothesis: if \cwm{} performance is capped by output-format constraints (exact string matching), seed-to-seed variability is naturally compressed relative to formulations whose performance depends more on learned representations.

